Z||000000||88 Fiero GT Turbo||02-23-2000||08:48 PM||||Hi guys I was wondering if you could give me some info on swaping the 2.8 GT with the 5 speed trany to 3.8 grand national motor with my trany.  If you could help by telliny me if there is any kits for this converison and if there are many fabercations and modifications to be made to the Fiero to do this converion.  Thanks for all the info.<P>Later,<BR>Jack||||reg||1
Z||000001||batboy||02-23-2000||10:00 PM||||Here is a place to start gathering some info. <P> <A HREF="http://www.americancustomeng.com/3800-V6.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.americancustomeng.com/3800-V6.htm</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||stimpy||02-23-2000||10:31 PM||||Grand National motor?  It would seem to me that you would want to start off with an engine that points in the correct direction. If you have a line on a boni-fide GN motor for cheap, buy it and resell it to a Buick Regal owner and finance your swap for a much more common and affordable fwd 3.8.  Did you want GN for the turbo? I don't know how that turbos work very well on the 3.8 in a fwd configuration, and all the engineering is already done on the supercharger thanks to GM.<BR>  Don't get me wrong, I'm not slamming you for bein creative and looking for a new way to skin a cat (ouch!) but I would hate for you to get taken by some smooth talkin salvage yard operator who would tell you that a 3.8 GN motor would "drop right in".  Buyer beware...especially when writing large checks in Colorado!||||reg||1
Z||000003||terryk||02-24-2000||12:03 PM||||It could be done although the turbo might hit the trunk wall. I know a guy that put a GN in an X-11 and it fit, so I would think it's possible for the Fiero.<P>To me, the advantage of a GN is the substantial boost capability that is not possible on the SC engines. I have an SC engine in my Ciera and I love it. I just know that a GN engine would slaughter it with some code tweaking.<P>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 02-24-2000).]<p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 02-24-2000).]||||reg||1
